#!/bin/sh
set -e

# python3-pillow conflicts with a file gl-sdk4-screen-large already owns (a
# bundled libfreetype), so it can't be a normal opkg Depends, and it can't
# be auto-installed from here either: opkg holds a non-reentrant lock for
# the whole transaction, so calling opkg (even just `list-installed`) from
# inside another package's postinst deadlocks on that same lock. Check via
# Python directly instead, and tell the user to run the one extra command
# themselves if it's missing.
if ! python3 -c "import PIL" 2>/dev/null; then
    cat <<'MSG'

NOTE: python3-pillow isn't installed, and can't be pulled in automatically
from here (see comment in postinst for why). Run this once before using
the dashboard:

  opkg install --nodeps python3-pillow

MSG
fi

chmod 755 /root/dashboard/*.py /root/dashboard/*.sh
chmod 755 /etc/init.d/citydash /etc/init.d/homebutton

/etc/init.d/homebutton enable
/etc/init.d/homebutton start

cat <<'MSG'

gl-e5800-dashboard installed. The stock GL.iNet screen is still active --
nothing has changed on the physical display yet.

Preview first (renders to PNGs, does not touch the live screen):
  python3 /root/dashboard/dashboard.py --preview /root/dashboard/preview

When ready to switch the physical screen over:
  /root/dashboard/toggle.sh on

To go back to the stock GL.iNet UI at any time:
  /root/dashboard/toggle.sh off
MSG

exit 0
